+        """Replace the vertices of shape ``pos`` in napari's shape list.
+
+        ``ShapeList.edit`` re-derives the displayed-shape bookkeeping and the
+        z-order of *all* shapes after every edit, which is O(N_visible) Python
+        work. A box edit keeps the shape's slice, z-index and triangulation,
+        so neither changes: the shape's vertices are updated in place and only
+        its rows of the displayed-vertex copy are refreshed. A changed
+        triangulation with the same counts (e.g. a box that becomes one voxel
+        thin) or a napari without these internals falls back to
+        ``ShapeList.edit``, which also rebuilds the displayed triangles. Other
+        counts (only a box with a zero extent has them) are left to a full
+        rebuild: ``ShapeList.edit`` would keep or move the shape's row slot,
+        which napari < 0.7 gets wrong, so ``_shapes_mode`` is cleared and the
+        caller rebuilds.
+        """
+        dv = self._data_view
+        shape = dv.shapes[pos]
